course: dictionary
lesson: 13115
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Flogging is one of them. Its meaning depends on the sentence around it, so use the context to choose the right one. «The captain gave the sailor a flogging with a whip.» Here the clues are whip and punishment, so it means a beating as a punishment.
explain: «Dad is flogging his old bike online.» Flogging here is informal talk for selling. Online and his old bike are the clues: people sell things online. Always test your meaning in the sentence. Does «Dad is beating his old bike online» make sense? No, so selling is the right meaning.
explain: «Our team got a flogging, losing 9-0.» In sport, a flogging is a heavy defeat. The score is the clue. Check the other meanings: a whip would make no sense on a football pitch, so the context points to a big loss.
fact: Flogging can mean a beating with a whip or stick, used as a punishment. This is an old, cruel punishment, and it is a sad part of history.
fact: In informal talk, flogging means selling: «flogging old toys» means selling old toys.
fact: In sport, especially in the UK, Australia and New Zealand, «a flogging» means a heavy defeat.
fact: Flogging is also the -ing form of the verb flog, so it can describe what someone is doing right now, like «Dad is flogging his bike».
fact: To choose the right meaning, look at the clues around the word and try each meaning in the sentence.
exercise: «The sailor was given a flogging with a whip for breaking the rules.» What does flogging mean here? | A big win in a game | A long walk | Selling something | *A beating as a punishment
exercise: «Dad is flogging his old bike online.» What does flogging mean? | Riding | Fixing | Painting | *Selling
exercise: «Our team got a flogging, losing 9-0.» What does flogging mean here? | Hit with a stick | *A heavy defeat | Cheering for the winners | A new kit
test: Sam says, «I am flogging my old games to my friends.» What does flogging mean? | Playing | *Selling | Giving away for free | Losing
test: Ella says, «We got a flogging at netball today.» What does she mean? | *We lost very badly | We were tired after the game | We won a prize | We played in the rain
exam: In «Dad is flogging his old bike online», which clue helps you know flogging means selling? | bike | is | *online | Dad
